 !include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
-title Private staged BOTH runtime transaction
-start
-:Issue fixed session / cursor operation to owned main and reference pipes;
-:Receive bounded closed JSON from both children;
-:Validate expected roles, message ordinals and recipient prefixes;
-:Compare independently produced canonical data;
-if (All checks pass?) then (yes)
-  :ACK the exact staged data to both owned children;
-  if (Both commit acknowledgements pass?) then (yes)
-    :Publish one BOTH successor;
-  else (no)
-    :Fail-stop both children without partial publication;
-    stop
-  endif
-else (no)
-  :Fail-stop both children without retry;
-  stop
-endif
-:Require close reply, stdin closure, bounded EOF and successful reap;
-note right
-  Parsing / hashes do not confer runtime authority.
-  Native proof cannot dispatch policy or learning work.
-  Synthetic transports are not F9 qualification.
+title BOTH source proof; archive approval UNUSED; selected local-clock protocol implementation pending
+
+participant "host-canonical-r4-source-1/canonical.ts\nverification4 SOURCE_ONLY PASS; review2 READY_SOURCE_ONLY" as TASK
+participant "packages/runtime/src/job.ts\nNativeJob unchanged" as JOB
+participant "packages/runtime/src/native-session.ts\nNativeSession unchanged" as SESSION
+participant "packages/runtime/src/process-transport.ts\nmain port: injected MOCK locally / real only future HOST" as MAIN
+participant "packages/runtime/src/process-transport.ts\nreference port: injected MOCK locally / real only future HOST" as REFERENCE
+
+group Injected local source proof - future HOST contract, not independent process execution or handoff
+  TASK -> TASK : reject supplied non-function factory BEFORE NativeJob construction or clock use
+  TASK -> TASK : SAME validated branch: absent/undefined -> fixedPort+REAL; callable -> injected+MOCK
+  TASK -> JOB : construct with original clock; work cutoff origin+10s /cleanup cutoff origin+300s
+  JOB --> TASK : original absolute deadlines; boot/startup cannot renew them
+  loop acquire main, then reference
+    TASK -> TASK : check original work deadline BEFORE this factory call
+    opt deadline reached before acquisition
+      break reject without invoking another factory
+        TASK -> TASK : stop only already-owned ports within original cleanup budget
+        TASK --> JOB : acquisition failure; no retry or partial success
+      end
+    end
+    alt main acquisition
+      TASK -> MAIN : validated factory(main); MOCK in local proof
+      MAIN --> TASK : return port; reject duplicate underlying ownership
+    else reference acquisition
+      TASK -> REFERENCE : SAME validated factory(reference); MOCK in local proof
+      REFERENCE --> TASK : return port; reject duplicate underlying ownership
+    end
+    TASK -> TASK : register distinct returned-port ownership BEFORE post-acquisition deadline check
+    opt original work deadline reached after return
+      break retain acquired-port ownership; admit no later factory
+        TASK -> TASK : stop owned ports within original origin+300s; preserve failure
+        TASK --> JOB : late acquisition fails; no clock reset
+      end
+    end
+  end
+  TASK -> SESSION : construct unchanged NativeSession with owned ports and original deadlines
+  JOB -> SESSION : fixed native-proof transaction; no policy/learning dispatch
+  SESSION -> MAIN : bind fixed owned session and role
+  SESSION -> REFERENCE : bind separately selected reference identity and role
+
+  loop three boundaries: init /open /empty settled
+    SESSION -> MAIN : fixed session/cursor operation; bounded closed JSON
+    SESSION -> REFERENCE : same operation; current-driver MOCK locally /independent reference REQUIRED for future HOST proof
+    MAIN --> SESSION : staged boundary/expected main role/message ordinal/recipient prefixes
+    REFERENCE --> SESSION : staged boundary/expected reference role/message ordinal/recipient prefixes
+    SESSION -> SESSION : validate closed schemas/roles/cursor/order/prefixes; compare canonical data
+    alt both staged boundaries valid and equal
+      SESSION -> MAIN : ACK exact staged data /commit
+      SESSION -> REFERENCE : ACK exact staged data /commit
+      MAIN --> SESSION : exact commit acknowledgement
+      REFERENCE --> SESSION : exact commit acknowledgement
+      alt both commit acknowledgements valid
+        SESSION --> JOB : publish ONE BOTH successor; no partial publication
+      else either commit acknowledgement fails
+        break reject transaction; admit no subsequent work
+          SESSION -> MAIN : fail-stop; no retry or partial successor
+          SESSION -> REFERENCE : fail-stop; preserve failure and partial facts
+          SESSION --> JOB : failure cleanup uses original300s cutoff; no reset
+        end
+      end
+    else either staged boundary fails or disagrees
+      break reject transaction; admit no subsequent work
+        SESSION -> MAIN : fail-stop; no retry
+        SESSION -> REFERENCE : fail-stop; no successor publication
+        SESSION --> JOB : failure cleanup uses original300s cutoff; no reset
+      end
+    end
+  end
+
+  SESSION -> MAIN : seventh exchange close; successful close within original10s
+  SESSION -> REFERENCE : seventh exchange close; no startup/work/close clock reset
+  MAIN --> SESSION : require close reply and separately captured finish facts
+  REFERENCE --> SESSION : require close reply and independently captured finish facts
+  SESSION -> SESSION : require EACH stdinClosed/stdoutEof/stderrEof/reaped/exit0/forced:false
+  SESSION --> JOB : accept only observed orderly close; never synthesize EOF from forced termination
+  JOB --> TASK : preserve original10s work /300s cleanup origin; no renewed stage budget
+end
+
+note over TASK,SESSION
+  Mock ports check staged commits and close facts
+  without starting either independent process.
+  These local checks cannot establish reference
+  agreement, native execution, or qualification
+  of the integrated game and model path.
 end note
-stop
